{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-4e961a0246489989994eaf605276c749f66fe43b28786d3c","family_id":"KR:012159","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Special Act on Investigating the Truth of the April 16 Sewol Ferry Disaster and Building a Safe Society","title_original":"4ㆍ16세월호참사 진상규명 및 안전사회 건설 등을 위한 특별법","kind":"법률","source_version":"284117","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=284117","source_sha256":"c141291f23520264444e31f7c7002ae169ff7b5f49b50f81aade863d8c364da6","body_sha256":"c0fd14d5a568fd9a9a1e4213736ab9b87725daa160fcdbfd385eb18a36e149f2","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 2 (Definitions)\nThe terms used in this Act shall be defined as follows: <Amended on Mar. 5, 2026>\n  1. The term “4/16 Sewol Ferry Disaster” means the tragedy that followed the sinking of the Sewol Ferry on April 16, 2014, in waters near Jodo-myeon, Jindo-gun, Jeonnam-Gwangju Integrated Special City, which caused a number of victims and sufferers;   \n  2. The term “victim” means a person who was aboard the Sewol Ferry at the time the 4/16 Sewol Ferry Disaster occurred, but who died or whose life or death is unknown, due to the disaster;  \n  3. The term “sufferer” means any of the following: \n  (a) Any person, other than a victim, who was aboard the Sewol Ferry at the time the 4/16 Sewol Ferry Disaster occurred (excluding those who, as a crew member of the Sewol Ferry, abandoned the ferry without taking necessary action to rescue passengers); \n  (b) The spouse, lineal ascendants or descendants, and siblings of a victim;\n  (c) The spouse, lineal ascendants or descendants, and siblings of a person falling under item (a).\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_title_re